cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. The base model is the ESC113M Group 03 course project (see references)."
title: "Jacketed Stirred-Tank Cooling: Dynamic Modelling, Reliability-Based Optimisation and Adaptive Operation"
version: "3.0.0"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nithin
    family-names: "D H"
    affiliation: "Department of Chemical Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nithindh2004/jacketed-stirred-tank-cooling-optimization"
keywords:
  - jacketed vessel
  - Runge-Kutta
  - Monte Carlo
  - chance-constrained optimisation
  - Sobol sensitivity
abstract: >-
  Simulation study of a jacketed stirred-tank cooling process. Coupled liquid
  and jacket-coolant energy balances are solved with RK4 and verified against
  the exact solution, then used for deterministic and chance-constrained
  optimisation of agitator speed and coolant flow, global sensitivity analysis,
  a simulated adaptive operating policy and model-form stress testing. Extends
  the ESC113M Group 03 course model. Code is MIT-licensed; reports, figures and
  data are CC BY 4.0; the original group materials are excluded (LICENSING.md).
references:
  - type: report
    title: "Cooling Dynamics of a Hot Liquid in a Well-Stirred Tank (ESC113M project report and MATLAB code)"
    authors:
      - name: "ESC113M Group 03, Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur"
    notes: "Original single-state RK4 model; included unchanged in docs/original_esc113m/ with the group members' permission."
